Loom: gfx1151 VALU source-bank placement preferences. An instruction reading two distinct VGPRs of one bank (mod 4)
issues in 2.5 cycles and three in 5 (measured, pure VALU; a VOPD pair counts both components), so the iu4 GEMM fold's
tied FMACs and scale products lost issue time next to the WMMAs. The tied FMAC (acc, a, b) and the two-source f32
add / sub / mul / fmaak now prefer pairwise different source banks in the instruction-aware allocation of 0031: three
reads of one bank in plain GEMM fold FMACs 21 -> 4, loop VGPRs 221 -> 213, WMMA banks unchanged. Bit-identical results;
pp2048 GEMM cycles -0.7% (gu -1.3%).
diff --git a/loom/py/loom/target/arch/amdgpu/descriptors/matrix.py b/loom/py/loom/target/arch/amdgpu/descriptors/matrix.py
